1
00:00:00,540 --> 00:00:01,940
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:03,710
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,710 --> 00:00:05,210
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,110 --> 00:00:07,380
(Episode 36)

5
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,320
You're Ko Eun Seol, right?

6
00:00:17,790 --> 00:00:18,790
Do I know you?

7
00:00:19,290 --> 00:00:21,360
I'm Na Hyun Hee,
Manager Na Tae Hoon's daughter.

8
00:00:25,330 --> 00:00:27,030
Manager Na Tae Hoon's...

9
00:00:28,370 --> 00:00:29,430
daughter?

10
00:00:29,870 --> 00:00:30,870
Yes.

11
00:00:31,540 --> 00:00:33,270
He was my dad,
and you're the reason he's dead.

12
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:37,610
I wanted to see you in person
at least once,

13
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:38,680
so I came by.

14
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:41,980
I wanted to see what kind of person
killed my dad.

15
00:00:45,820 --> 00:00:48,150
I think you have the wrong idea.

16
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:50,790
What happened to Manager Na...

17
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,790
wasn't because of me.

18
00:00:54,430 --> 00:00:56,390
If you hadn't shown up,

19
00:00:57,800 --> 00:00:59,500
my dad wouldn't have died.

20
00:01:02,300 --> 00:01:03,370
My dad...

21
00:01:04,570 --> 00:01:06,740
would never make that kind of choice
and leave me behind.

22
00:01:06,970 --> 00:01:07,970
Just you wait.

23
00:01:08,870 --> 00:01:10,610
I'll uncover everything someday.

24
00:01:17,780 --> 00:01:18,820
Wait.

25
00:01:27,930 --> 00:01:28,930
Are you okay?

26
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:47,150
This season's new arrivals
seem better.

27
00:01:48,910 --> 00:01:51,220
Although, it might not quite match
your skin tone.

28
00:01:52,520 --> 00:01:53,550
Do you have any other colors?

29
00:01:54,150 --> 00:01:56,350
You've already seen
all the other colors.

30
00:01:58,390 --> 00:01:59,390
Did I?

31
00:02:01,860 --> 00:02:04,330
The new arrivals here seem
a bit predictable.

32
00:02:05,960 --> 00:02:07,670
Should we go somewhere else?

33
00:02:07,970 --> 00:02:09,170
Hae Ra, that's enough.

34
00:02:11,070 --> 00:02:12,140
How many hours has it been?

35
00:02:22,010 --> 00:02:24,950
My outfit for this dinner event
is pretty dressy,

36
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:27,920
so you need to step up your game.

37
00:02:28,790 --> 00:02:31,190
Come on, let's check out
one last store.

38
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:33,760
I don't exist
just to make you look good.

39
00:02:37,630 --> 00:02:39,360
Am I your arm candy?

40
00:02:40,300 --> 00:02:41,870
What do you mean by arm candy?

41
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:45,600
We're a couple,
so matching our outfits is nice.

42
00:02:46,500 --> 00:02:47,870
Whenever you act like this,

43
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:49,610
I feel like
I'm just a decorative prop.

44
00:02:49,870 --> 00:02:52,380
Are you crazy?
Why would I think of you like that?

45
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:54,110
Do you have to say it that way?

46
00:02:54,410 --> 00:02:55,410
If that isn't it,

47
00:02:56,750 --> 00:02:58,720
just accept me for who I am.

48
00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:01,790
Stop trying so hard to dress me
in all these high-end brands.

49
00:03:05,290 --> 00:03:06,290
Seok Jin!

50
00:03:14,970 --> 00:03:16,870
Mr. Seok Jin, is that you?

51
00:03:17,940 --> 00:03:19,640
Oh. Hi, Hae Ra.

52
00:03:20,570 --> 00:03:22,140
Mom, I'll get changed first.

53
00:03:22,540 --> 00:03:23,540
Okay.

54
00:03:36,050 --> 00:03:38,460
Fine. I'm sorry.

55
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:41,230
From now on,
I'll decide your outfit first...

56
00:03:41,330 --> 00:03:43,560
and match mine to yours. Okay?

57
00:03:44,960 --> 00:03:46,260
Please don't be mad.

58
00:03:47,900 --> 00:03:49,970
Do we have to coordinate
our outfits like that?

59
00:03:50,440 --> 00:03:52,570
Can't we just dress normal,

60
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:54,570
like we usually do around people?

61
00:03:55,040 --> 00:03:57,740
Being normal is the scarier part.

62
00:03:58,210 --> 00:04:00,380
Looking good is normal
for rich kids,

63
00:04:00,450 --> 00:04:02,880
but when you have nothing,
normal means looking broke.

64
00:04:04,350 --> 00:04:05,350
So,

65
00:04:05,850 --> 00:04:09,090
because I have nothing,
normal means worn down?

66
00:04:11,060 --> 00:04:13,120
No, that's not what I meant.

67
00:04:13,930 --> 00:04:17,430
You need to dress appropriately
for the time and place.

68
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:20,870
Besides, you know how my dad is.

69
00:04:21,330 --> 00:04:23,800
Being criticized in front of others
is something he absolutely hates.

70
00:04:27,210 --> 00:04:30,240
So just bear with it,
even if it's uncomfortable.

71
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:33,310
This is all a way to score points
with my dad.

72
00:04:34,610 --> 00:04:35,610
Okay?

73
00:04:42,920 --> 00:04:43,920
I'll get going.

74
00:04:44,920 --> 00:04:45,920
You don't need to see me out.

75
00:04:52,460 --> 00:04:54,170
Why? What now?

76
00:04:54,470 --> 00:04:56,400
Did you apologize to Mr. Seok Jin?

77
00:04:57,100 --> 00:04:58,100
What's it to you?

78
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:01,810
Since you apologized, have an apple.

79
00:05:04,080 --> 00:05:06,110
Ms. Park, are you making fun of me
right now?

80
00:05:07,350 --> 00:05:09,050
Read the room, will you?

81
00:05:09,580 --> 00:05:10,750
My apple!

82
00:05:14,850 --> 00:05:18,320
I gave her an apple
because she apologized.

83
00:05:20,760 --> 00:05:23,230
I don't like Hae Ra at all.
I hate her.

84
00:05:24,160 --> 00:05:25,800
I won't play with her.

85
00:05:30,770 --> 00:05:33,370
You're not some accessory
or arm candy.

86
00:05:34,070 --> 00:05:35,340
You're the prized possession...

87
00:05:35,870 --> 00:05:37,540
of Kang Hae Ra,
successor to Cheongma Group.

88
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:41,950
I'm going to make you mine...

89
00:05:42,680 --> 00:05:45,480
and keep you on display next to me
for the rest of my life.

90
00:05:52,390 --> 00:05:54,890
You're giving this to me?

91
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:57,060
Why?

92
00:05:58,400 --> 00:05:59,460
Well, why else?

93
00:06:00,430 --> 00:06:04,600
Consider it our way of asking you
to be a good boss to Eun Guk.

94
00:06:06,040 --> 00:06:07,140
Yes, exactly.

95
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:10,270
We aren't the kind of people
who lack basic manners.

96
00:06:11,480 --> 00:06:15,280
I see.
Then I'll gratefully accept it.

97
00:06:15,480 --> 00:06:16,480
- Wait.
- Well...

98
00:06:17,850 --> 00:06:20,750
Since you'll be cooking it anyway,
you'll let us have a taste, right?

99
00:06:21,620 --> 00:06:22,620
Excuse me?

100
00:06:22,690 --> 00:06:25,060
Mom, why are you so blunt about it?

101
00:06:25,790 --> 00:06:29,030
I mean, surely Teun Teun's Mom
won't eat this all by herself.

102
00:06:29,090 --> 00:06:32,500
There is so much meat here,
so it's only right to share it.

103
00:06:32,860 --> 00:06:34,200
Right, Mi Rae?

104
00:06:36,370 --> 00:06:37,370
I knew it.

105
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:40,440
There's no way you'd just
give this to me as a gift.

106
00:06:40,910 --> 00:06:45,280
You want me to take these ribs
and cook them for you.

107
00:06:45,810 --> 00:06:48,380
- You catch on quickly.
- Gosh, no.

108
00:06:48,680 --> 00:06:52,080
I told you it's a gift.
While you're cooking it,

109
00:06:52,320 --> 00:06:53,580
maybe just save a plate for us?

110
00:06:54,320 --> 00:06:56,850
You see, our Eun Guk
absolutely loses his mind...

111
00:06:56,990 --> 00:06:58,690
when it comes to short ribs.

112
00:07:01,060 --> 00:07:03,800
I'll cook some for you
when I get some free time.

113
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:06,760
- We can eat them together then.
- Sounds good, yes.

114
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,730
We can wait as long as it takes.

115
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:10,400
Right, Mom?

116
00:07:10,570 --> 00:07:13,540
Well, it's better than
letting it all go to waste.

117
00:07:13,770 --> 00:07:15,210
A hundred times better.

118
00:07:25,050 --> 00:07:26,780
If you hadn't shown up,

119
00:07:27,720 --> 00:07:29,290
my dad wouldn't have died.

120
00:07:37,430 --> 00:07:38,430
What?

121
00:07:38,730 --> 00:07:40,570
Manager Na's daughter, Na Hyun Hee?

122
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:43,530
Yes, I heard it clearly.

123
00:07:46,470 --> 00:07:50,910
I always knew she would show up
at least once someday.

124
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:54,650
So what happened between them?

125
00:07:54,950 --> 00:07:56,910
She must have been preparing
and waiting for this,

126
00:07:57,250 --> 00:07:59,450
because she just poured it all out
on Ko Eun Seol.

127
00:08:00,020 --> 00:08:01,850
She said her dad died
because of Eun Seol.

128
00:08:02,450 --> 00:08:04,160
It seemed like she was...

129
00:08:04,690 --> 00:08:07,190
holding Ko Eun Seol responsible
for Manager Na's death.

130
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:11,030
Why wouldn't she?
She's not entirely wrong.

131
00:08:11,930 --> 00:08:14,970
Manager Na killed
Ko Eun Seol's mother.

132
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:18,070
Manager Na was afraid
of getting caught,

133
00:08:18,340 --> 00:08:19,700
so he took his own life.

134
00:08:20,170 --> 00:08:23,170
Then Ko Eun Seol spent
ten years in prison...

135
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:25,440
because of Manager Na.

136
00:08:30,780 --> 00:08:35,420
Manager Na made a last-ditch effort
to drag me down with him.

137
00:08:36,250 --> 00:08:39,760
He tried to frame me
for murdering Ko Eun Seol's mother.

138
00:08:42,130 --> 00:08:43,160
I see.

139
00:08:44,030 --> 00:08:45,130
Therefore,

140
00:08:45,800 --> 00:08:49,800
keep a close eye on both Ko Eun Seol
and Manager Na's daughter.

141
00:08:50,740 --> 00:08:52,270
Don't let this blow back on me.

142
00:08:52,970 --> 00:08:55,070
Yes, I'll watch them closely.

143
00:08:55,610 --> 00:08:57,010
And send some consolation money...

144
00:08:57,070 --> 00:08:59,010
to Manager Na's daughter
under my name.

145
00:08:59,810 --> 00:09:02,910
We need to placate her with money
so there's no trouble later.

146
00:09:03,750 --> 00:09:05,380
Yes, understood.

147
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:11,520
(Head of Legal Affairs,
Seo Hyun Jae)

148
00:09:11,520 --> 00:09:13,220
She eventually came looking for you.

149
00:09:15,330 --> 00:09:16,330
Yes.

150
00:09:17,130 --> 00:09:19,060
Did you know about this,
Attorney Seo?

151
00:09:20,670 --> 00:09:23,970
I tried to talk to her,
but she didn't make it easy.

152
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:25,770
The look in her eyes...

153
00:09:26,940 --> 00:09:29,570
reminded me exactly of my past self.

154
00:09:31,210 --> 00:09:33,540
The hatred and resentment
toward the world.

155
00:09:35,110 --> 00:09:36,810
I could see it all in her eyes.

156
00:09:41,650 --> 00:09:42,850
This won't do, Eun Seol.

157
00:09:44,890 --> 00:09:48,060
You shouldn't concern yourself
with Manager Na's case anymore.

158
00:09:50,490 --> 00:09:51,500
As it happens,

159
00:09:51,560 --> 00:09:53,030
the detective in charge
of Manager Na's case...

160
00:09:53,100 --> 00:09:54,800
is my high school friend.

161
00:09:56,530 --> 00:09:57,800
I'll look into it further.

162
00:09:58,370 --> 00:09:59,370
I think it'd be best...

163
00:09:59,540 --> 00:10:01,810
if you stepped away from this
for the time being.

164
00:10:05,580 --> 00:10:07,980
(Summary of Evidence
and Suicide Note)

165
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:10,350
(1. Original Suicide Note)

166
00:10:18,960 --> 00:10:22,930
The police have already decided
to close the case,

167
00:10:22,990 --> 00:10:24,530
so there's nothing more to dig into.

168
00:10:25,930 --> 00:10:29,230
Manager Na Tae Hoon
wrote the suicide note himself?

169
00:10:29,670 --> 00:10:31,440
Yes, the handwriting analysis...

170
00:10:31,470 --> 00:10:33,170
confirmed it was him.

171
00:10:35,310 --> 00:10:36,510
What about his movements
before the incident?

172
00:10:36,910 --> 00:10:40,240
The lack of activity
makes it a bit suspicious.

173
00:10:40,980 --> 00:10:41,980
What do you mean?

174
00:10:42,550 --> 00:10:46,250
The accounts he mainly used
were all burner accounts.

175
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:48,050
When we traced the accounts,

176
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:50,790
most of the money
had been sent overseas.

177
00:10:53,660 --> 00:10:54,990
Was there anything else?

178
00:10:55,560 --> 00:10:57,430
His daughter in high school and...

179
00:10:57,530 --> 00:10:59,700
Director Joo Mi Ran, was it?

180
00:11:00,430 --> 00:11:02,800
Other than them,
he didn't contact anyone else.

181
00:11:04,670 --> 00:11:05,770
Director Joo?

182
00:11:06,670 --> 00:11:08,970
I believe her birth name
was Joo Ae Sook.

183
00:11:09,870 --> 00:11:11,980
We questioned her
during the investigation.

184
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:15,110
Her alibi for that day was solid,

185
00:11:16,050 --> 00:11:18,420
and there was no sign of blackmail
in their call logs.

186
00:11:22,990 --> 00:11:24,690
Regarding Director Joo Mi Ran,

187
00:11:25,060 --> 00:11:26,490
can I take a look at the profile?

188
00:11:26,790 --> 00:11:27,860
Hey,

189
00:11:27,930 --> 00:11:30,230
I could get fired
for showing you that.

190
00:11:32,030 --> 00:11:33,360
Just do me a solid, will you?

191
00:11:38,300 --> 00:11:39,900
We've only got a few days...

192
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,310
until the scholarship foundation's
board meeting.

193
00:11:42,010 --> 00:11:44,040
To get the new scholarship program
approved,

194
00:11:44,110 --> 00:11:45,940
we need a majority vote.

195
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:48,210
Eun Seol,

196
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:51,120
where are we on analyzing
the board members' votes?

197
00:11:51,450 --> 00:11:53,520
Based on my research,
quite a few directors sympathize...

198
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:55,920
with the purpose
of the scholarship program.

199
00:11:56,320 --> 00:11:59,460
Besides them, there are about
three people who are neutral,

200
00:11:59,760 --> 00:12:02,990
and their decisions will be crucial
for passing the agenda.

201
00:12:04,660 --> 00:12:06,400
You're right. With these three,

202
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:08,670
we won't know for sure
until the very end.

203
00:12:09,730 --> 00:12:12,440
However, for the sake
of a fair evaluation,

204
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:13,940
there must be absolutely
no direct contact...

205
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:15,910
with the board members.

206
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:20,440
As this is
the first scholarship program...

207
00:12:20,680 --> 00:12:22,680
I've spearheaded,

208
00:12:23,580 --> 00:12:26,250
I don't want to be evaluated
based on my title as chairman.

209
00:12:27,220 --> 00:12:31,490
I want our scholarship program
to be evaluated on its own merits...

210
00:12:31,860 --> 00:12:33,790
and yield good results.

211
00:12:34,590 --> 00:12:35,590
Of course.

212
00:12:35,890 --> 00:12:38,060
I understand what you mean, ma'am.

213
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:43,330
I could push the project through
on my own authority.

214
00:12:44,440 --> 00:12:45,770
But if I do that,

215
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:49,710
we're ignoring the very spirit
and values of this foundation.

216
00:12:50,980 --> 00:12:54,310
I'll be keeping my distance
from the board members as well for now.

217
00:12:54,610 --> 00:12:57,350
So, to keep rumors at bay,

218
00:12:57,850 --> 00:12:59,520
you should avoid
any unnecessary contact...

219
00:12:59,950 --> 00:13:01,920
with the board members.

220
00:13:02,290 --> 00:13:04,720
- Understood?
- Yes, we'll do that.

221
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,320
Will do.

222
00:13:09,290 --> 00:13:10,290
Eun Seol.

223
00:13:12,860 --> 00:13:14,300
Is everything all right?

224
00:13:15,900 --> 00:13:17,330
Did you get home safely yesterday?

225
00:13:18,270 --> 00:13:20,200
Yes. Nothing happened.

226
00:13:23,010 --> 00:13:25,940
Then I'll treat you to lunch today.

227
00:13:26,740 --> 00:13:28,480
To help you get your energy back,

228
00:13:28,550 --> 00:13:30,950
let me treat you
to a whole meal of healthy food.

229
00:13:32,180 --> 00:13:34,650
I think I'll pass today.

230
00:13:35,550 --> 00:13:36,790
I'll take a rain check on lunch.

231
00:14:07,790 --> 00:14:08,790
Director Joo,

232
00:14:09,220 --> 00:14:11,590
what time is the lunch appointment
with CEO Son?

233
00:14:12,520 --> 00:14:13,760
It's at 12:30 p.m.

234
00:14:16,530 --> 00:14:17,530
Let's go.

235
00:14:27,140 --> 00:14:28,510
(CEO Kang Young Hoon)

236
00:14:28,570 --> 00:14:32,440
You must be busy lately
with the premium food hall project.

237
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:34,250
Yes, indeed.

238
00:14:34,480 --> 00:14:35,950
Being busy is great,

239
00:14:36,280 --> 00:14:38,780
but things are pretty chaotic
with everything happening all at once.

240
00:14:43,450 --> 00:14:44,490
Here.

241
00:14:44,990 --> 00:14:47,360
I owe it all to you, Director Joo.

242
00:14:48,390 --> 00:14:49,430
Not at all.

243
00:14:49,890 --> 00:14:52,600
It's all thanks to your ability
to read the board.

244
00:14:55,100 --> 00:14:57,400
Just opening in this department store
isn't enough.

245
00:14:57,670 --> 00:15:00,400
We need to prove ourselves
through our sales.

246
00:15:01,110 --> 00:15:03,510
That's the only way
to knock my wife off her high horse.

247
00:15:05,180 --> 00:15:08,980
My wife is too tied down
by my father-in-law's...

248
00:15:08,980 --> 00:15:10,710
outdated values.

249
00:15:11,880 --> 00:15:14,490
I don't know how long
she plans to lead Cheongma...

250
00:15:14,550 --> 00:15:16,320
with those old-fashioned values.

251
00:15:18,190 --> 00:15:21,190
In that sense,
you're truly amazing, sir.

252
00:15:22,190 --> 00:15:23,190
What?

253
00:15:23,730 --> 00:15:26,230
All of Cheongma's current success...

254
00:15:26,430 --> 00:15:28,270
isn't from riding
the former chairman's coattails,

255
00:15:28,430 --> 00:15:30,900
but entirely down
to your own capabilities.

256
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:36,410
The future history of Cheongma
will belong to you,

257
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:37,980
not the former chairman.

258
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:40,480
That's right.

259
00:15:41,610 --> 00:15:42,880
That's how it must be.

260
00:15:50,350 --> 00:15:52,290
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

261
00:15:52,490 --> 00:15:54,390
- Seok Jin, are you good to go?
- Yes.

262
00:15:55,160 --> 00:15:57,730
You put up a fight,
but you still wore it anyway.

263
00:15:58,000 --> 00:15:59,100
Should I take it off?

264
00:15:59,330 --> 00:16:01,670
Why would you
when it looks so good on you?

265
00:16:02,330 --> 00:16:03,870
- Let's go.
- What about the CEO?

266
00:16:04,270 --> 00:16:06,270
He'll come straight from dinner
with Jae Seong's dad.

267
00:16:06,740 --> 00:16:07,740
Okay, let's go.

268
00:16:11,780 --> 00:16:13,540
I can't believe that woman.

269
00:16:14,180 --> 00:16:16,680
What if they eat all those ribs
by themselves?

270
00:16:17,380 --> 00:16:19,950
I doubt Teun Teun's mom
would do that.

271
00:16:20,420 --> 00:16:22,790
She'll at least offer us
a plate to sample.

272
00:16:25,990 --> 00:16:28,190
What is it? Do you smell something?

273
00:16:28,290 --> 00:16:29,290
The smell of ribs?

274
00:16:29,390 --> 00:16:30,790
Hold on a second.

275
00:16:31,730 --> 00:16:34,000
I think I smell meat.

276
00:16:35,530 --> 00:16:36,630
I smell it, too.

277
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:42,240
Hold on. This smells like doenjang.

278
00:16:44,510 --> 00:16:47,110
Dummy, that's your own feet
you're smelling.

279
00:16:47,310 --> 00:16:49,010
Wash your feet properly.

280
00:16:49,410 --> 00:16:50,480
They stink.

281
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:52,950
Is that so?

282
00:16:54,950 --> 00:16:57,250
I can't believe you.

283
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:59,020
You complete fool.

284
00:17:09,630 --> 00:17:11,070
Look who it is.

285
00:17:12,140 --> 00:17:15,170
It's the princess of Cheongma,
Team Leader Kang Hae Ra.

286
00:17:16,040 --> 00:17:17,570
What's with the flattery?

287
00:17:19,810 --> 00:17:20,810
You made it.

288
00:17:21,480 --> 00:17:24,110
Even Cheongma's loyal subject,
Chief Cha,

289
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:27,480
has graced this humble place
with his presence.

290
00:17:29,150 --> 00:17:30,390
I'm truly honored.

291
00:17:33,660 --> 00:17:34,660
Director Min.

292
00:17:38,500 --> 00:17:40,060
The newly launched whiskey...

293
00:17:40,730 --> 00:17:42,130
is getting quite a lot of buzz.

294
00:17:42,800 --> 00:17:44,030
Thank you, sir.

295
00:17:45,340 --> 00:17:46,770
Once the business stabilizes,

296
00:17:47,300 --> 00:17:50,310
won't we start hearing talk
about your marriage?

297
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:55,050
Judging by what Chairman Min said,
he seems to have a plan.

298
00:17:55,380 --> 00:17:57,280
I wouldn't mind marrying right now.

299
00:17:58,580 --> 00:18:00,780
If only I could find someone
like Hae Ra.

300
00:18:02,120 --> 00:18:03,120
What are you saying?

301
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:05,260
Then, step it up.

302
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:09,360
I have no intention...

303
00:18:09,960 --> 00:18:11,660
of giving
my precious daughter away...

304
00:18:11,960 --> 00:18:13,530
to some guy
who might make her suffer.

305
00:18:15,330 --> 00:18:17,270
If your new business
gets good reviews,

306
00:18:17,940 --> 00:18:19,340
I'll think about it.

307
00:18:20,370 --> 00:18:21,770
Sure. Watch and see
how well I deliver.

308
00:18:22,710 --> 00:18:24,610
There's someone
I'd like to introduce to you today.

309
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:25,680
Please come this way.

310
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:51,970
Hey, Cha Seok Jin.

311
00:18:56,810 --> 00:18:58,340
Your position doesn't seem
all that secure.

312
00:19:02,380 --> 00:19:03,480
What do you mean?

313
00:19:05,650 --> 00:19:08,520
So you're not Cheongma's
prospective son-in-law,

314
00:19:08,790 --> 00:19:10,990
but just a candidate
for the position.

315
00:19:11,620 --> 00:19:15,090
Man, I thought you already set
a wedding date.

316
00:19:17,930 --> 00:19:21,430
If I had known, I would've tried
to score some points with Hae Ra.

317
00:19:23,770 --> 00:19:25,270
Her father said it's not too late.

318
00:19:26,040 --> 00:19:28,170
I should work hard to catch up.

319
00:19:31,580 --> 00:19:32,910
As if you ever could.

320
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:36,310
You'll just stretch yourself
too thin.

321
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:38,380
What did you say, you punk?

322
00:19:38,550 --> 00:19:40,880
The CEO isn't a pushover.

323
00:19:43,350 --> 00:19:45,520
Unlike your dad, I mean.

324
00:19:46,790 --> 00:19:49,390
He won't just accept everything
because you whine.

325
00:20:00,500 --> 00:20:02,170
I have no intention...

326
00:20:02,170 --> 00:20:03,840
of giving
my precious daughter away...

327
00:20:03,910 --> 00:20:05,580
to some guy
who might make her suffer.

328
00:20:20,090 --> 00:20:21,560
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

329
00:20:21,630 --> 00:20:23,290
Why on earth
is my dad acting like this?

330
00:20:23,890 --> 00:20:26,700
Even if he didn't exactly love you
from the start,

331
00:20:26,800 --> 00:20:27,930
it was never this bad.

332
00:20:29,730 --> 00:20:31,900
Did you step out of line
without me knowing?

333
00:20:33,070 --> 00:20:35,470
- Step out of line, how?
- Then what's gotten into him?

334
00:20:37,370 --> 00:20:38,640
Could this all be a strategy?

335
00:20:38,740 --> 00:20:39,810
What strategy?

336
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:43,410
Provoking you for no reason
so you treat me better...

337
00:20:43,810 --> 00:20:45,020
or something like that.

338
00:20:45,120 --> 00:20:46,320
Unbelievable.

339
00:20:47,480 --> 00:20:50,150
So, especially at times like this,
you need to treat me better.

340
00:20:50,450 --> 00:20:52,120
That way, you won't get
on his bad side anymore.

341
00:20:54,320 --> 00:20:55,890
The answer is already set, then.

342
00:20:56,390 --> 00:20:59,300
I'll also look for a way
for you to score some points.

343
00:21:01,670 --> 00:21:03,630
Your dad really said that?

344
00:21:04,030 --> 00:21:05,370
Yes, he did.

345
00:21:05,570 --> 00:21:09,410
He told Jae Seong he could
even marry me if he did well,

346
00:21:09,570 --> 00:21:11,110
as if he wanted Seok Jin to hear it.

347
00:21:11,940 --> 00:21:14,750
Your dad's been so off lately.

348
00:21:15,550 --> 00:21:17,710
I have no idea
why he's turned so cold.

349
00:21:18,220 --> 00:21:22,050
Mom, can't you support Seok Jin
a little?

350
00:21:22,790 --> 00:21:23,790
Me?

351
00:21:24,520 --> 00:21:27,290
How could I possibly help?

352
00:21:28,060 --> 00:21:29,360
His business needs
to hit the jackpot...

353
00:21:29,430 --> 00:21:31,160
for Dad to truly acknowledge him.

354
00:21:32,360 --> 00:21:34,460
Mom, be the face
of our new shoe brand.

355
00:21:35,670 --> 00:21:37,500
Me, as the face of the brand?

356
00:21:38,000 --> 00:21:40,440
You haven't been as active lately,
but you're still an actress.

357
00:21:40,840 --> 00:21:44,110
Can't you at least give Seok Jin
your full backing?

358
00:21:44,840 --> 00:21:46,440
- Mom, please.
- Gosh.

359
00:21:47,440 --> 00:21:48,810
All right, I'll do it.

360
00:21:49,210 --> 00:21:50,910
I guess it isn't that hard.

361
00:22:06,660 --> 00:22:08,470
Do you see that?
Those forearm muscles?

362
00:22:09,730 --> 00:22:11,570
They just flexed.

363
00:22:11,670 --> 00:22:13,900
For some reason,
I feel like the coffee he makes...

364
00:22:13,970 --> 00:22:15,310
will be super strong.

365
00:22:15,870 --> 00:22:17,410
Enough to make my head spin.

366
00:22:18,610 --> 00:22:21,110
It might not be caffeine,
but some kind of drug in it.

367
00:22:21,450 --> 00:22:23,210
I think I'm going to be
completely addicted.

368
00:22:27,220 --> 00:22:28,320
I'll do it.

369
00:22:31,860 --> 00:22:33,190
Here's your coffee.

370
00:22:37,430 --> 00:22:40,630
Hey, the boss looks a bit old.

371
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:43,900
I know. She looks really old, right?

372
00:22:49,310 --> 00:22:50,540
I bet you heard all that.

373
00:22:51,580 --> 00:22:52,580
Heard what?

374
00:22:52,910 --> 00:22:54,380
Come on, you heard everything.

375
00:22:54,380 --> 00:22:56,910
Those high schoolers earlier
chattering about your muscles.

376
00:22:58,650 --> 00:23:00,580
Well, that's nothing new to me.

377
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:03,090
Have you been showing off
on purpose?

378
00:23:04,120 --> 00:23:05,390
Why would I need to do that?

379
00:23:06,320 --> 00:23:07,320
Besides,

380
00:23:08,260 --> 00:23:10,190
this is all just
good business tactics...

381
00:23:10,260 --> 00:23:11,460
and marketing, right?

382
00:23:12,700 --> 00:23:15,100
From now on, stay in the kitchen
when high schoolers come in.

383
00:23:16,530 --> 00:23:17,530
What?

384
00:23:19,340 --> 00:23:21,540
Speaking as a parent,

385
00:23:21,610 --> 00:23:24,110
it's really not good
for their education.

386
00:23:25,640 --> 00:23:27,910
Come on, kids these days
grow up fast.

387
00:23:28,410 --> 00:23:31,410
And while proper education
is important,

388
00:23:31,780 --> 00:23:34,250
isn't sales revenue
what matters most?

389
00:23:35,350 --> 00:23:39,260
Actually, I was thinking about
passing out cafe flyers...

390
00:23:39,260 --> 00:23:40,460
right in front of the school.

391
00:23:41,120 --> 00:23:43,790
Don't do it. Don't you dare.

392
00:23:48,930 --> 00:23:50,030
Hello, ma'am.

393
00:23:50,100 --> 00:23:52,200
Hey, are you just getting in?

394
00:23:52,300 --> 00:23:53,340
Yes.

395
00:23:54,400 --> 00:23:55,570
Are you waiting for Eun Seol?

396
00:23:55,640 --> 00:24:00,110
A grown woman should know better
than to stay out so late.

397
00:24:03,850 --> 00:24:05,580
That sounds like concern to me.

398
00:24:06,880 --> 00:24:09,690
It's not like I hated Eun Seol
from the very beginning.

399
00:24:10,350 --> 00:24:11,350
You know, don't you?

400
00:24:12,090 --> 00:24:14,990
My daughter-in-law
took her in and raised her.

401
00:24:16,090 --> 00:24:17,560
Yes, I know.

402
00:24:18,130 --> 00:24:20,860
Apparently, Eun Seol was
her high school friend's daughter.

403
00:24:21,300 --> 00:24:24,200
Her birth mother is some woman
named Joo Ae Sook.

404
00:24:27,540 --> 00:24:29,770
I believe her birth name
was Joo Ae Sook.

405
00:24:32,480 --> 00:24:35,680
Eun Guk's mother ran into that friend
at the hospital,

406
00:24:36,050 --> 00:24:39,180
but the woman just dumped the baby
and disappeared.

407
00:24:39,850 --> 00:24:41,990
So my daughter-in-law
took the baby in and raised her.

408
00:24:43,050 --> 00:24:44,050
Oh, right.

409
00:24:44,420 --> 00:24:47,060
Isn't there a Joo Mi Ran
where you work?

410
00:24:48,290 --> 00:24:49,290
Yes.

411
00:24:49,360 --> 00:24:51,230
- Do you mean Director Joo Mi Ran?
- Yes, her.

412
00:24:52,030 --> 00:24:54,900
At first, I thought
she might be Eun Seol's mother,

413
00:24:55,200 --> 00:24:56,670
so I went to see her once.

414
00:24:58,100 --> 00:25:01,000
Wait.
You must never tell Eun Seol. Never.

415
00:25:01,840 --> 00:25:05,310
If Eun Guk's father finds out,
he'll throw another huge fit.

416
00:25:06,580 --> 00:25:07,580
Understood.

417
00:25:07,980 --> 00:25:10,310
Did you say you came by our company?

418
00:25:10,310 --> 00:25:12,520
Yes. But while I was there,

419
00:25:13,350 --> 00:25:15,890
I found out that she isn't actually
Eun Seol's biological mother.

420
00:25:16,690 --> 00:25:21,290
Darn it, I went for nothing
and lost the maternity handbook.

421
00:25:23,030 --> 00:25:25,600
Still, it's not like
I need it anymore anyway.

422
00:25:26,800 --> 00:25:28,130
A maternity handbook?

423
00:25:28,430 --> 00:25:30,230
Yes, it belonged
to Eun Seol's biological mother.

424
00:25:30,770 --> 00:25:32,740
It's the handbook from
when she had Eun Seol.

425
00:25:34,640 --> 00:25:37,540
Do you happen to remember
the name of the hospital?

426
00:25:37,810 --> 00:25:40,210
I read it so many times,
of course I remember.

427
00:25:41,510 --> 00:25:43,580
It was Taeseon Hospital, I think.

428
00:25:45,380 --> 00:25:46,550
Taeseon Hospital?

429
00:25:46,950 --> 00:25:48,020
Mom.

430
00:25:48,750 --> 00:25:50,220
Mom, where did you go again?

431
00:25:50,320 --> 00:25:53,060
Listen, just pretend
you never heard any of this.

432
00:25:53,220 --> 00:25:55,930
You can never tell Eun Seol, okay?

433
00:25:56,390 --> 00:25:57,630
Of course. Got it.

434
00:25:58,430 --> 00:26:02,200
All right. I'm coming.
I can't leave for even a second.

435
00:26:06,700 --> 00:26:08,370
Taeseon Hospital?

436
00:26:13,780 --> 00:26:16,750
So Director Joo was
your mother's classmate?

437
00:26:17,550 --> 00:26:20,350
Yes, and not just any classmate.

438
00:26:20,520 --> 00:26:22,250
I think they were pretty close.

439
00:26:37,300 --> 00:26:38,870
(Taeseon Hospital)

440
00:26:40,300 --> 00:26:42,270
(Joo Ae Sook, 128-4 Eunpa-Dong,
Guwon-gu, Haseong)

441
00:26:46,810 --> 00:26:47,910
What the heck?

442
00:26:48,650 --> 00:26:51,280
Then Director Joo
is Eun Seol's biological mother?

443
00:26:52,750 --> 00:26:53,820
No way.

444
00:26:55,720 --> 00:26:57,150
But while I was there,

445
00:26:57,890 --> 00:27:00,520
I found out that she isn't actually
Eun Seol's biological mother.

446
00:27:02,590 --> 00:27:03,660
Exactly.

447
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:07,230
I should dig some more for now.

448
00:27:09,800 --> 00:27:12,170
Is her beauty ready to shine?
Okay, here we go.

449
00:27:13,570 --> 00:27:16,470
One, two, three.
Yes, show the shoes a bit more.

450
00:27:16,870 --> 00:27:18,140
Looks good.

451
00:27:18,880 --> 00:27:21,080
Great. Let's keep going.

452
00:27:23,910 --> 00:27:24,980
Yes, perfect.

453
00:27:26,080 --> 00:27:27,080
One, two, three.

454
00:27:35,630 --> 00:27:37,130
It's been a while
since I shot anything,

455
00:27:37,190 --> 00:27:39,060
so I felt a bit awkward.

456
00:27:39,530 --> 00:27:41,770
Not at all.
You were completely natural.

457
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:44,870
You pulled off the product better
than any other model.

458
00:27:45,940 --> 00:27:47,640
Right, I have to agree with that.

459
00:27:48,040 --> 00:27:50,540
It reminded me
that my mom was an actress.

460
00:27:51,140 --> 00:27:52,180
Really?

461
00:27:53,210 --> 00:27:55,180
Still, I'm not as good
as I used to be.

462
00:27:56,450 --> 00:27:57,710
Thanks to you,

463
00:27:57,750 --> 00:27:59,750
I think our sales
will noticeably increase.

464
00:27:59,750 --> 00:28:01,990
That would be wonderful.

465
00:28:02,790 --> 00:28:05,120
Anyway, Dad's been really strange.

466
00:28:05,360 --> 00:28:07,460
Lately, he has been giving Seok Jin
a hard time for no reason.

467
00:28:08,630 --> 00:28:11,390
So, Mom, give Seok Jin
your full support.

468
00:28:11,730 --> 00:28:14,330
After all, you're the largest shareholder
in Cheongma.

469
00:28:14,330 --> 00:28:17,400
Aren't you the one
who actually owns Cheongma, not Dad?

470
00:28:18,300 --> 00:28:21,140
Come on. Why would you say that?

471
00:28:22,210 --> 00:28:25,110
Mom, you'll back Seok Jin, right?

472
00:28:26,040 --> 00:28:29,250
Of course. It isn't just anyone.

473
00:28:29,680 --> 00:28:32,720
It's our Chief Cha,
so of course I'll help.

474
00:28:33,880 --> 00:28:35,150
- Chief Cha.
- Yes?

475
00:28:35,990 --> 00:28:39,320
If you ever need help in the future,
tell me anytime.

476
00:28:40,390 --> 00:28:42,090
With Hae Ra's father
being so demanding,

477
00:28:42,160 --> 00:28:44,430
I figured you were already
having a hard time.

478
00:28:45,630 --> 00:28:47,760
I really want things...

479
00:28:48,030 --> 00:28:50,400
to go well for you, Chief Cha.

480
00:28:51,070 --> 00:28:52,240
Thank you, ma'am.

481
00:28:53,640 --> 00:28:54,640
You know, right?

482
00:28:55,240 --> 00:29:00,040
You were the dream and hope
of the Cheongma Scholarship Foundation.

483
00:29:02,650 --> 00:29:05,820
I'm rooting for you in many ways.

484
00:29:07,620 --> 00:29:10,520
I'll definitely live up
to your expectations.

485
00:29:11,090 --> 00:29:12,090
Okay.

486
00:29:15,160 --> 00:29:17,330
Did you prepare the gifts
for the foundation's board members?

487
00:29:17,590 --> 00:29:19,860
Yes, I plan to hand them out
starting today.

488
00:29:20,860 --> 00:29:23,700
We have to lock in those board votes
before the meeting.

489
00:29:23,900 --> 00:29:26,440
They must not lean toward
voting in favor.

490
00:29:27,200 --> 00:29:30,010
Since it's the CEO's will,
all the board members will agree.

491
00:29:30,640 --> 00:29:31,940
I see. Then...

492
00:29:32,980 --> 00:29:37,110
By the way, how is
An Guk Cheol doing these days?

493
00:29:38,350 --> 00:29:39,480
There's nothing new.

494
00:29:39,850 --> 00:29:42,750
He doesn't deviate an inch
from the plan I set up.

495
00:29:43,450 --> 00:29:45,790
He takes the bait
without any suspicion,

496
00:29:47,060 --> 00:29:49,630
and he seems easier to tame
than I thought.

497
00:29:50,460 --> 00:29:52,530
Okay, I got it. You can go now.

498
00:29:59,500 --> 00:30:01,240
An easy guy to tame?

499
00:30:05,410 --> 00:30:07,210
(Cheongma Scholarship Foundation)

500
00:30:07,210 --> 00:30:09,380
(PR Director Joo Mi Ran)

501
00:30:14,320 --> 00:30:17,190
(127-8 Bohyeon-ro, Jungsan-gu,
Seoul, Eden Motel)

502
00:30:17,420 --> 00:30:21,320
(Director's Office)

503
00:30:22,890 --> 00:30:24,030
Secretary Choi...

504
00:30:29,270 --> 00:30:30,930
(Director's Office)

505
00:30:33,170 --> 00:30:35,070
For the sake of a fair evaluation,

506
00:30:35,310 --> 00:30:37,470
there must be absolutely
no direct contact...

507
00:30:37,470 --> 00:30:38,640
with the board members.

508
00:30:40,340 --> 00:30:43,050
What is Secretary Choi doing?

509
00:30:44,510 --> 00:30:46,250
All right.

510
00:30:46,250 --> 00:30:48,420
Just deal, man. No cut.

511
00:30:48,620 --> 00:30:50,950
- No cut?
- Deal.

512
00:30:50,950 --> 00:30:53,490
- Wish you luck.
- The luck is mine.

513
00:30:53,560 --> 00:30:56,460
All right, come to me.

514
00:31:02,470 --> 00:31:03,470
Fold.

515
00:31:03,870 --> 00:31:05,270
You're folding again?

516
00:31:06,040 --> 00:31:07,870
I can fold if my hand is bad.

517
00:31:07,870 --> 00:31:11,870
How can we keep our game going
if you fold all the time?

518
00:31:11,940 --> 00:31:13,180
Stop picking a fight with me.

519
00:31:13,240 --> 00:31:14,580
I can fold if my hand is bad.

520
00:31:14,580 --> 00:31:18,150
Still, a game is only good
if there's a decent pot.

521
00:31:18,210 --> 00:31:20,420
- You haven't changed at all.
- Deal the cards again.

522
00:31:20,420 --> 00:31:23,420
This guy plays by zero rules.
Seriously, what's wrong with you?

523
00:31:23,490 --> 00:31:25,320
- Why do you always fold?
- Deal again.

524
00:31:25,320 --> 00:31:28,060
Deal again?
Why are you ruining the game?

525
00:31:28,120 --> 00:31:29,730
Deal, jerk.
Let's reset and go again.

526
00:31:29,790 --> 00:31:30,790
Reset, my foot.

527
00:31:37,600 --> 00:31:38,600
Ae Sook.

528
00:31:39,570 --> 00:31:40,700
Did you come to see me?

529
00:31:55,020 --> 00:31:56,090
Let go of me.

530
00:31:57,650 --> 00:31:58,720
It's me.

531
00:32:00,260 --> 00:32:02,790
Ae Sook, you haven't changed a bit.

532
00:32:04,060 --> 00:32:05,090
Let go.

533
00:32:05,300 --> 00:32:06,300
Let go!

534
00:32:29,320 --> 00:32:33,020
(A Trap Called Desire)

535
00:32:33,090 --> 00:32:35,660
I'm thinking of taking
some of your workload.

536
00:32:35,730 --> 00:32:37,260
I don't mean anything else by it.

537
00:32:37,590 --> 00:32:39,500
I'll check out the school first.

538
00:32:39,900 --> 00:32:42,330
I was wondering how it would be
to move your mother here.

539
00:32:42,600 --> 00:32:44,830
Do you think doing this
will make Seok Jin choose you?

540
00:32:44,900 --> 00:32:47,140
Can't you get Ms. Park away
from Seok Jin?

541
00:32:47,800 --> 00:32:49,910
I hate his mother so much!

542
00:32:50,340 --> 00:32:53,540
It won't be long
until we become a perfect family.

543
00:32:53,880 --> 00:32:55,610
Everything will soon be mine.

544
00:32:55,610 --> 00:32:58,680
Did you ever have a meal alone
with my husband,

545
00:32:58,680 --> 00:32:59,820
just the two of you?

546
00:33:00,020 --> 00:33:02,620
Mention the name Joo Ae Sook
one more time,

547
00:33:02,690 --> 00:33:05,360
and I'll personally bury you
in concrete.

548
00:33:06,320 --> 00:33:08,320
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
